        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.closer/text": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-005-Appetite-Choice.yaml",
          "value": "Remember, from this moment forward,\nyou will recognize your body's genuine\nneed for nourishment and remain in control\nof your eating decisions.\n\nWhenever you wish to release an unnecessary\ncraving or desire for food, simply pause.\n\nInhale and gently hold your breath.\n\nSilently say to yourself,\n\"{{ cue.primary }}.\"\n\nThen slowly exhale through your mouth,\nas though gently blowing out a candle.\n\nThis concludes your OCF Appetite Choice exercise.",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.closer/text"
        },
        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.closer/version": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-005-Appetite-Choice.yaml",
          "value": "1.3.0",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.closer/version"
        },
        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/cue_template/allowed/0": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-005-Appetite-Choice.yaml",
          "value": "cue.primary",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/cue_template/allowed/0"
        },
        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/cue_template/function_id": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-005-Appetite-Choice.yaml",
          "value": "OCF-BOD-005",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/cue_template/function_id"
        },
        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/status": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-005-Appetite-Choice.yaml",
          "value": "reviewed",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/status"
        },
        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/text": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-005-Appetite-Choice.yaml",
          "value": "From this moment forward, you will have greater\ncontrol over your appetite and your desire for food.\n\nYou will recognize the difference between your body's\ngenuine need for nourishment and the passing desire\nto eat out of habit, boredom, or impulse.\n\nYour mind and body will work together in harmony,\nhelping you make clear, confident decisions\nabout when and what you choose to eat.\n\nWhen your body needs nourishment, you will recognize\nthat need clearly and respond appropriately.\n\nWhen a temporary craving arises and you consciously\nchoose not to eat, you will remain calm,\ncomfortable, and in complete control of your decision.\n\nFrom this moment forward, this awareness\nwill become a natural and automatic part\nof your everyday life.\n\nYou will find it easier to recognize when you\nhave eaten enough, to enjoy the food you choose,\nand to stop eating when you are comfortably satisfied.\n\nYour choices will become clearer,\nyour habits more intentional,\nand your confidence stronger.\n\nWhenever you wish to release a passing craving\nor an unnecessary desire for food,\nyou can do so quickly and easily.\n\nSimply pause and bring your awareness\nto the desire you wish to release.\n\nTake a comfortable breath in\nand gently hold it.\n\nWhile holding your breath, silently\nsay to yourself, \"{{ cue.primary }}.\"\n\nThen slowly exhale through your mouth,\nas though gently blowing out a candle.\n\nAs you exhale, the unnecessary desire to eat\nwill become less and less important to you.\n\nYour thoughts will become calm and clear.\n\nYou will feel satisfied with your decision\nand free to direct your attention\ntoward whatever you choose.\n\nFood will no longer demand your attention\nsimply because it is present,\nbecause you see it, or because you smell it.\n\nYou will remain free to enjoy food\nwhen you consciously choose to eat.\n\nYour body will continue to communicate\nits genuine needs clearly and naturally.\n\nYou will respond to those needs with confidence,\nmaintaining the nourishment and balance\nyour body requires.\n\nNow know that this pattern of conscious choice\nis becoming firmly established within you.\n\nFrom this moment forward, your ability\nto recognize unnecessary cravings\nand release them will operate automatically.\n\nYour mind will naturally pause before\nhabitual or impulsive eating,\nallowing you to make a clear decision.\n\nYou will feel comfortable and confident\nchoosing when to eat and when to wait.\n\nEach time you use {{ cue.primary }},\nyour ability to release unnecessary cravings\nbecomes easier, smoother, and more effective.\n\nRemember, your appetite is something\nyou can understand and consciously direct.\n\nYou will recognize your body's needs,\nmake your decisions clearly,\nand remain in control of your choices.\n\nThis lasting pattern of awareness,\nsatisfaction, and self-control\nwill continue strengthening every day.",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/text"
        },
        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-005.function-body/version": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-005-Appetite-Choice.yaml",
