        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-exp-002.function-body/text": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-EXP-002-Insulate.yaml",
          "value": "From this moment forward, you have the ability\nto create a balanced zone of temperature comfort\nsurrounding your entire physical body.\n\nWhenever you desire this protection,\nimagine a continuous, even layer of insulation\nextending around you from head to toe.\n\nInhale deeply and gently hold your breath.\n\nThink or say in your mind, \"{{ cue.primary }}.\"\n\nThen exhale slowly through your mouth.\n\nYour zone will immediately begin to form,\nsurrounding you in a smooth, balanced field\nadjusted to the comfort you desire.\n\nWhen the surroundings are cold,\nthe zone will resist excessive cooling,\nconserving comfortable warmth around your body.\n\nWhen the surroundings are hot,\nthe zone will resist excessive heating,\nmaintaining a comfortable, balanced condition.\n\nAs the environment changes, your zone\nwill adjust continuously and evenly,\nstrengthening or easing its insulating effect\naccording to what is needed.\n\nYour physical body and your total self\nwill work together in this pattern of balance,\nmaintaining the zone without constant attention.\n\nThe ability to use Insulate is now\npermanently available whenever you choose,\nand the selected zone continues operating\nuntil you consciously change or release it.\n\nTo cancel the current temperature adjustment,\ninhale, hold your breath, think or say\nin your mind, \"{{ cue.id.OCF-CMD-EXP-002-CANCEL }},\" then exhale.\n\nThat adjustment will end, leaving you free\nto establish a different one whenever desired.\n\nWhen you wish to place the entire Insulate\napplication on hold, bring Insulate into your mind.\nInhale, hold your breath, think or say\nin your mind, \"{{ cue.id.OCF-CMD-EXP-002-RELEASE }},\" then exhale.\n\nThe present zone will rest, while your ability\nto create it remains ready for future use.\n\nEach time you use Insulate, establishing\nand adjusting your zone will become\neasier, smoother, and more effective.",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-exp-002.function-body/text"
        },
