        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-sen-001.function-body/text": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-SEN-001-Hearing.yaml",
          "value": "From this moment forward, you have the ability\nto regulate your hearing and develop vivid,\nclear sound within your imagination.\n\nYour hearing will respond to your intention.\nYou can bring subtle sounds into clearer awareness\nor allow unwanted sounds to fade into the background.\n\nTo enhance your hearing, close your eyes,\ninhale deeply, and gently hold your breath.\nThink or say in your mind, \"{{ cue.primary }}.\"\nThen exhale slowly through your mouth and open your eyes.\n\nFaint sounds will become clearer and more distinct.\nYou will notice delicate differences in pitch,\ntone, rhythm, and sounds both high and low.\nYour awareness will recognize the sounds\nyou wish to hear with greater ease.\n\nTo reduce unwanted sound, use the same eye\nand breathing sequence, thinking or saying,\n\"{{ cue.id.OCF-CMD-SEN-001-HEAR-LESS }}.\"\nDistracting sounds will become less prominent,\nwhile you remain free to change the adjustment\nor return to your usual hearing condition.\n\nYour inner sense of hearing will also grow stronger.\nYou will recall familiar voices, melodies,\nconversations, and sounds of places you remember.\nEven in silence, you can imagine a voice speaking,\nmusic playing, or a sound moving through space.\n\nYou can hold an inner sound clearly, hear its\npitch and rhythm, change its volume or tone,\nand create new combinations through imagination.\nYou will recognize the difference between sounds\nyou imagine and sounds around your physical body.\n\nThis ability to remember and create sound within\nyour mind will become a permanent part of your total self.\nWhenever you choose, these commands can strengthen\nan imagined sound or allow it to gently fade.\n\nEach time you use this function, your hearing regulation\nand inner auditory imagery will become easier,\nclearer, and more effective.",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-sen-001.function-body/text"
        },
